-- title:
--   Existence of dual endomorphisms in the rational endomorphism subring
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with an $F$-algebra structure, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $F$ which is elliptic. Write $P = (W_{/k})(k)$ for the group of affine points, i.e. the points of the base change of $W$ to $k$ in Weierstrass (affine) form, and let $S$ be [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalEndSubring k W`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L32), the subring of $\mathrm{End}(P)$ (the additive endomorphisms of $P$, with multiplication given by composition) generated by the set of those additive maps $\alpha \colon P \to P$ which are either $0$ or satisfy the predicate `IsRationallyRepresented k W W`. The conclusion is the predicate [`DualIsogenyExistence`](def/DualIsogenyAPI.html#L274) for $S$: for every $\varphi \in S$ there exist an additive endomorphism $\hat\varphi$ of $P$ and integers $t$ and $n$ such that $\varphi + \hat\varphi = [t]$, $\varphi \hat\varphi = [n]$ and $\hat\varphi \varphi = [n]$ in $\mathrm{End}(P)$, where $[m]$ denotes the multiplication-by-$m$ map, and moreover $\hat\varphi$ again lies in $S$ and $n \ge 0$. In particular every element of $S$ satisfies a monic integral quadratic relation $\varphi^2 - [t]\varphi + [n] = 0$ with $n \ge 0$.
--
--   This is the existence of the dual isogeny together with its trace and norm identities, in the form of a closure property of the subring of rationally represented endomorphisms: the degree provides a non-negative integral norm compatible with composition. It is the geometric input for the structure results on this subring, being cited by [`WeierstrassCurve.free_and_finrank_rationalEndSubring_eq_four`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.free_and_finrank_rationalEndSubring_eq_four), [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_mem_rationalHomSet_isDualPair_and_add_eq_smul_id`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_mem_rationalHomSet_isDualPair_and_add_eq_smul_id) and [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_anticommuting_pair_mem_rationalHomSet_of_frobenius_eq_smul`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_anticommuting_pair_mem_rationalHomSet_of_frobenius_eq_smul).
